<DocsLayout title="Introduction" pathname="/docs" section="Getting started">
  <h1>Your AI agents are temporary. The system that <em>governs</em> them shouldn&rsquo;t be.</h1>
  <p class="dx-lede">
    Máddu is the external record that verifies what your AI agents did, so no agent is ever
    the sole witness to its own work. It&rsquo;s a local-first, files-only spine that any CLI
    coding agent plugs into to work as an auditable team: one agent per lane, risky changes
    held behind approvals, every slice checked by a gate. No cloud, no telemetry, no key
    interception.
  </p>

  <div class="dx-note">
    <span class="dx-note-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◆</span>
    <p><strong>Tracing tools observe runs. Memory tools remember. Máddu governs how agents collaborate</strong> — it's the discipline layer, not another dashboard.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <p>From any git repo with Node.js ≥ 20, one command installs the runtime, cockpit, and state directory. It touches only <code>.maddu/</code>, <code>maddu/</code>, and <code>maddu.json</code> — nothing else in your tree.</p>

  <div class="dx-code">
    <div class="dx-code-head"><span class="dx-code-dot"></span> terminal</div>
    <pre><code><span class="tok-c"># install the latest from GitHub</span>
npx github:frdyx/maddu init

<span class="tok-c"># verify the install + hard rules</span>
maddu doctor</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>
    Everything reduces to <strong>one substrate loop</strong>. Each transition writes exactly
    one event to the append-only spine on disk, so any run replays end to end.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>register</strong> — a session joins the record</li>
    <li><strong>claim</strong> — a lane is locked so two agents never touch the same files</li>
    <li><strong>slice</strong> — a unit of work runs under that lane</li>
    <li><strong>stop</strong> — the slice closes with a receipt</li>
    <li><strong>release</strong> — the lane frees for the next agent</li>
    <li><strong>close</strong> — the session leaves the record</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>One default execution path</h3>
  <p>
    The slash and autopilot surfaces are friendly wrappers over that same loop — never
    competing flows. A non-trivial task defaults to a <em>pipeline</em>; ad-hoc autopilot is
    reserved for genuine one-offs.
  </p>

  <h2>The guarantees</h2>
  <p>Nine hard rules govern the framework layer and are verified by <code>maddu doctor</code> on every run:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Files-only state · append-only spine · no hosted backends</li>
    <li>No provider SDKs in framework code · no token export</li>
    <li>Three-layer brand boundary · lane ownership</li>
    <li>Every auto-trigger crosses the gauntlet — permanent</li>
  </ul>

